
<head>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <link href="~/css/Modal.css" rel="stylesheet" />
    <style>
        .codesnippet {
            background: darkslategray;
            margin-bottom: 0;
        }

            .codesnippet p {
                color: white;
                margin-bottom: 0;
            }

            .codesnippet span {
                color: cornflowerblue;
            }

            .codesnippet span2 {
                color: palegreen;
            }

        /*This does work but is not needed*/
        /*.codesnippet span.green {
                color: palegreen;
            }*/

    </style>
</head>

<div class="col-sm-12" align="center" style="border-radius: 20px; padding:10px; align-items: center;">
    <div class="row" align="center" style="word-wrap: break-word; font-weight: bold; padding-top: 10px;">
        <h1 style="word-wrap: break-word; font-weight: bold;">PC Launcher Documentation</h1>
    </div>
</div>
<br />

@*Background*@
<div class="col-sm-12" style="border-radius:20px; padding:10px; align-items:center;">
    <h3>Background</h3>
    <hr />
    <p>
        This is documentation on how to use the Febris PC Launcher. Start by downloading the PC package from the Febris Portal.
    </p>
    <p style="font-weight:bold">
        Not every aspect of the Febris PC Launcher is optimal.
        The PC software does not currently have a signing certificate.
        This will change in future releases.
    </p>
</div>

@*Requirements*@
<div class="col-sm-12" style="border-radius: 20px; padding:10px; align-items: center;">

    <h3>Requirements</h3>
    <hr />
    <p>
        Needed Items:
    </p>
    <ol>
        <li>
            VR ready PC running Windows 10 (Windows 11 may work but is untested)
        </li>
        <li>
            Compatible headset and accompanying hardware
        </li>
    </ol>
</div>

@*Registering Device*@
<div class="col-sm-12" style="border-radius: 20px; padding:10px; align-items: center;">

    <h3>Registering a device</h3>
    <hr />
    <p>
        Registration of the device in the Febris system manages the automation of module distribution and data collection.
        The software needs to be running on the new PC before attempting to register it in your hardware system.
    </p>
    <p>
        Go to the configuration page and find the hardware license.
        This series of letters a numbers will be used when creating hardware on the Febris portal.
    </p>
</div>
@*Image*@
<div class="container-fluid" align="center">

    <img src="~/images/DocumentationImages/PCLauncher/PCConfig_License.png" alt="Device Registration" width="50%" />
    @*<div>
            <img src="@Url.Action("DocumentationImageLoader","Widget",new {path=Model.ScreenShot1})" alt="Device Setup" />
        </div>*@
    <p class="italic">PC Registration</p>
</div>

@*Setup*@
<div class="col-sm-12" style="border-radius: 20px; padding:10px; align-items: center;">

    <h3>Setting up your device</h3>
    <hr />
    <p>
        Currently there is no need to provide log in credentials for launcher operations. So please do not feel any need to provide them.
    </p>
    <p>
        If you are a developer setup is as simple as selecting the developer option and saving the selection.
        From here on the device should be connected to your company’s account.
    </p>
    <p>
        If you are not a developer than the proper URL needs to be setup.
        Your IT administrator will have set up a private URL for your Febris operations.
        The URL can vary from a prefix, path, or port.
        If you do not know what these are please ask your IT Administrator.
        If the category does not exist, leave the section blank.
    </p>
</div>
@*Image*@
<div class="container-fluid" align="center">

    <img src="~/images/DocumentationImages/PCLauncher/PCConfig_Save.png" alt="Launcher Config" width="50%" />

    @*<div>
            <img src="@Url.Action("DocumentationImageLoader","Widget",new {path=Model.ScreenShot1})" alt="Device Setup" />
        </div>*@
    <p class="italic">Launcher Config</p>
</div>



